{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <i>Dlin sequence</i>, the first term is a positive integer and each term after the first is calculated by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the previous term in the sequence, then doubling the result. For example, the first seven terms of the Dlin sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab734f0d1d149f394bac30bed297bd11a88a924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 10, 22, 46, 94, 190, 382$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all possible first terms which give a Dlin sequence that includes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8a2f37be700ea1af2ea6c8397a908448ae4f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1406$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa62a365c27d4f2c298262b3e8c7c224550c20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> term of the Dlin sequence. We can realize that for the sequence to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8a2f37be700ea1af2ea6c8397a908448ae4f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1406$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, either the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8a2f37be700ea1af2ea6c8397a908448ae4f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1406$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> or one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8a2f37be700ea1af2ea6c8397a908448ae4f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1406$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8a2f37be700ea1af2ea6c8397a908448ae4f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1406$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d64905b03985e013fb87d75c555a247e810d1842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1406}{2} - 1 = 703 - 1 = 702$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/62584147a400cad55d24562c8c194d449306d8af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{n + 1}}{2} - 1 = a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"34\" /> in the sequence.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2f549965059c7e2b65c4366cfe542fc8fb8789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$702$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb9515ff6fc80eecaf202f9eb838967cad434df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{702}{2} - 1 = 351 - 1 = 350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"199\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceffeb3d880c80aa8bb29fe99a7905ca0b2f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a5d6acf2e5c02300001a3944b00fa6910b1f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{350}{2} - 1 = 175 - 1 = 174$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"199\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a1bf1111b9288bbee8699ee4e9503017e9a42f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$174$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c3599d99d564a7d110ad789cb6da250d9a2f304c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{174}{2} - 1 = 87 - 1 = 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c6169a64f8271966651402df19345f38ae0c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f0b9c862497d9fdeccd042269f8ad6e214c9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{86}{2} - 1 = 43 - 1 = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68b0e2e1efcac526f0ace05c6813fe0cab46be71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{42}{2} - 1 = 21 - 1 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If one of the later terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the term before that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150993088d49d7316f75a5e7590a9fc1cc655176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{2} - 1 = 10 - 1 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"38\" />. This is an odd number and halving it would result in a non-integer number, so this is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85fde30f8782973603ebed5bea5197a4578ad72e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{9, 20, 42, 86, 174, 350, 702, 1406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"252\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012759\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 452/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4957/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.700      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    7.700      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36615:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012759 and revision id 282457. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}